2	 "gdd": "design/gdd/chart-table-web-map-and-menus.md",
3	 "blockers": [
4	  {
5	   "where": "AC-CT-102 (L1900) vs Tuning Knobs 'Coupled constraints' header (L1100-1102), rows C-1, C-5, C-6, C-7, C-8, C-9 (L1106-1114) and AC-CT-127 (L1920)",
6	   "issue": "The ADR-0007 s2.5 amendment to AC-CT-102 now says a value outside its published safe range is neither clamped nor refused, and that only CONTENT_FIELD_RANGE or CONTENT_INVARIANT refuse a load, 'never a clamp'. The coupled-constraints section was not updated. Its header says each constraint is enforced 'by a clamp (with a log line) or a refusing assert'. Rows C-1, C-5, C-6, C-8 and C-9 prescribe clamps, and C-7 prescribes 'refusing assert / clamp'. AC-CT-127 (BLOCKING) tests the clamp ('satisfied after the documented clamp', 'RING_STEP_MIN_CHANNEL 6 is clamped to 3'). An implementer cannot satisfy AC-CT-102 and AC-CT-127 together, and writing the clamps breaks ADR-0007 s2.5. The only clamps left in the GDD are the runtime frame-delta clamp (UI_DT_MAX_MS, CT-43), which is a different thing and fine.",
7	   "fix": "Rewrite the coupled-constraints header, C-1, C-5 to C-9 and the AC-CT-127 text. Each constraint becomes a named structural invariant declared in the config schema and refused at load as CONTENT_INVARIANT(table, name). A clamp-and-log fix is dropped. C-2, C-3 and C-10 already refuse, so keep them. C-4 keeps its layout lint. Change AC-CT-127's expected outcomes from 'clamped to 3' to 'refused with CONTENT_INVARIANT'. Alternatively, restate AC-CT-102 to exempt load-time coupled-constraint clamps, but that contradicts ADR-0007 s2.5, so the first option is preferred. Also keep AC-CT-127's 'range minima and maxima' sweep consistent with the rule that a published range is guidance only."
8	  }
9	 ]
10	}

